aiHub-prefs-description = Multi-vendor AI plugin: literature summaries, smart annotations, Q&A chat, translation / mindmap / review, plus an embedded MCP server bridging external AI clients.
aiHub-prefs-open-dashboard = Open AI Hub Settings
aiHub-prefs-open-dashboard-help = Opens the full settings dashboard for providers, features, RAG and the embedded MCP server.
aiHub-prefs-howto = Quick start:
  1. Add a provider: click the button above to open the settings, then pick a provider type (OpenAI / DeepSeek / Qwen / ERNIE / Kimi / local Ollama, etc.) and click "+ Add provider".
  2. Fill it in: enter the API key in that row, select or type the default model, then click "Test" to verify connectivity (green check = OK).
  3. Make it default: tick "Enabled" and click the radio button in the Actions column; adjust "Priority" to control failover order.
  4. Save: always click the green "Save Settings" button at the bottom and wait for the "Saved N providers" confirmation.
  5. Use it: AI summary, annotation, chat, translate, mindmap and review are available from the Zotero toolbar / context menu.
  Tip: if the dropdown seems unresponsive, first pick a provider in the "Type" dropdown, then click the arrow of the "Default model" field to choose a model, then click "Save Settings".
